                <owl:onClass>
                    <owl:Class>
                        <owl:complementOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/PaN/NeXus/definitions#NX_CHAR"/>
                    </owl:Class>
                </owl:onClass>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:comment>
        The reference point of the aperture is its center in the x and y axis. The reference point on the z axis is the
        surface of the aperture pointing towards the source.

        In complex (asymmetric) geometries an NXoff_geometry group can be used to provide an unambiguous reference.

        .. image:: aperture/aperture.png
            :width: 40%
      </rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://manual.nexusformat.org/classes/base_classes/NXaperture.html#nxaperture-depends-on-field"/>
        <rdfs:label>NXaperture/depends_on</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://manual.nexusformat.org/classes/base_classes/NXaperture.html#nxaperture-depends-on-field"/>
    </owl:Class>
    


