                <owl:onClass>
                    <owl:Class>
                        <owl:complementOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/PaN/NeXus/definitions#NX_FLOAT"/>
                    </owl:Class>
                </owl:onClass>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:comment>
        This is the flight path before the sample position. This can be determined by a chopper,
        by the moderator, or the source itself. In other words: it is the distance to the component
        which gives the T0 signal to the detector electronics. If another component in the
        NXinstrument hierarchy provides this information, this should be a link.
      </rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://manual.nexusformat.org/classes/applications/NXtofraw.html#nxtofraw-entry-pre-sample-flightpath-field"/>
        <rdfs:label>NXtofraw/ENTRY/pre_sample_flightpath</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://manual.nexusformat.org/classes/applications/NXtofraw.html#nxtofraw-entry-pre-sample-flightpath-field"/>
    </owl:Class>
    


